- An offline edit of a `pendingInit` workspace keeps `pendingInit`, so a later relocate accepts the moved folder (`apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:634`) — "Change folder…" works for a workspace that was renamed while its drive was away. The rename survives the move. If it fails: If the moved folder already holds an identity with another id, the probe adopts that id (lines 718-727) and the offline edit is lost. Before this change that case came out as `different`. The earlier… Evidence: `apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:603-638`, `apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:702-727`, `apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:733-749`, `apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:850-856`, `apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry-relocate.test.ts:221-243`.

